# Rank 1519 / CVE-2023-28326: OpenMeetings' invitation dialog enabled
# its personal-URL generate button whenever exactly one recipient was
# selected, without checking who the recipient was, so an inviter could
# generate a personal access URL for an ordinary user and bypass the
# intended permission path (broken access control, CWE-863; OPENMEETINGS-
# 2739; the advisory records CWE-306 for the same access-control family).
# updateButtons in openmeetings-web/src/main/java/org/apache/openmeetings/
# web/common/InvitationForm.java did
# `dialog.getGenerate().setEnabled(recpnts.size() == 1)` -- the condition
# covers the count but not the principal: generating a URL is legitimate
# only for the inviter's own account (WebSession.getUserId()) or a
# CONTACT-type user. The fixing commit 1fb71af36 ("[OPENMEETINGS-2739]
# generate URL is disabled if non-contact is selected"): generateEnabled
# starts false and turns true only when the single recipient satisfies
# `getUserId().equals(u.getId()) || User.Type.CONTACT == u.getType()`.
#
# ATTENTION, capability-gate completeness. The guard exists and runs --
# its condition names the wrong principal vocabulary (count, not
# type/identity), the same decision-completeness family as ranks 1540
# (permission-switch branches), 1556 (sibling route groups) and 1567
# (submit paths without the form token): nothing can ask "does the
# enabled-state condition of a capability cover the principal types
# allowed to exercise it" -- UI component state is not authorization
# vocabulary anywhere in the corpus. A binding on OpenMeetings' own
# dialog would detect this application rather than the weakness.
#
# Re-probed at the recheck span tip, which carries every definition and
# engine change shipped since the first pass. Path 1 does not convert:
# the AUTH additions since the first pass (VYQL-AUTH-160 through
# VYQL-AUTH-179) are logout invalidation, result staging, admission
# policy, host validation, ignored-authorization-result and their kin --
# none names a UI component's enabled state, and no concept in
# ontology/ or review/concepts/review/ is about component state at all
# (the nearest authz-shaped review concepts -- AuthorizationCheck,
# IgnoredAuthorizationResult, BackendRouteMissingModuleAuthorization --
# are route, endpoint and permission-API concepts; Wicket's
# updateButtons is none of those). Measured 3x --cache off /
# timeout 180 / --max-ram 6GB per revision on the real checkout,
# vulnerable parent 1fb71af36^ against fix 1fb71af36:
#
#   openmeetings-web/src/main/java/org/apache/openmeetings/web/common/
#   InvitationForm.java -- 0/0/0 findings naming the file at BOTH
#   revisions, full findings view, deterministic; the whole repository
#   reports 646 findings at the vulnerable revision and 646 at the fix
#   with 314 at or above high each, and no delta row touches the file.
#   The flags view carries exactly one flag on the file at both
#   revisions: core.ResourceRelease on dialog.close at line 248, a
#   control fact outside updateButtons. vyql match on the file labels
#   nothing in the method at all -- no source, no sink, no control; the
#   only labels are log.error sinks at lines 237 and 245. A hard zero
#   in both views, not a misread one.
#
# Path 3 is not shippable today, measured on this very tree: setEnabled
# is called 99 times across 611 Java files, and only four of those
# calls are gated on a size or emptiness test -- the vulnerable
# generate, its sibling getSend().setEnabled(!recpnts.isEmpty()) in the
# same target.add(...) statement, RoomInvitationForm's
# getSend().setEnabled(!to.isEmpty()) for the group case, and
# MessagesContactsPanel's deleteBtn.setEnabled(!selectedMessages.isEmpty())
# over the session user's own messages. Three of the four are correct
# code: they gate capabilities whose exercise never touches another
# principal's account. A shape-only rule over the count condition
# therefore fires backwards on this tree, and the discriminator it is
# missing is exactly the ontology piece named above -- which principals
# a gated capability may be exercised against. Narrowing instead on
# OpenMeetings' own dialog accessor or on the fix's inline-expression
# spelling would be a repro-shaped patch keying the fixing commit's
# layout. No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1519 records the
# count-only condition, the principal-checked form and the three safe
# count-gated controls from the same tree, all asserting reject
# VYQL-AUTH-079: when capability-gate vocabulary lands, the count-only
# form must flip to expect and the three safe forms must stay reject.

test "rank1519: the generate button trusts the count alone"
  lang java
  file openmeetings-web/src/main/java/org/apache/openmeetings/web/common/InvitationForm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.openmeetings.web.common;

  import java.util.Collection;

  public abstract class InvitationForm extends Form<Invitation> {
      protected void updateButtons(AjaxRequestTarget target) {
          Collection<User> recpnts = recipients.getModelObject();
          target.add(
                  dialog.getSend().setEnabled(!recpnts.isEmpty())
                  , dialog.getGenerate().setEnabled(recpnts.size() == 1)
                  );
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1519: the fixed revision gates the button on the principal"
  lang java
  file openmeetings-web/src/main/java/org/apache/openmeetings/web/common/InvitationForm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.openmeetings.web.common;

  import java.util.Collection;

  public abstract class InvitationForm extends Form<Invitation> {
      protected void updateButtons(AjaxRequestTarget target) {
          Collection<User> recpnts = recipients.getModelObject();
          boolean generateEnabled = false;
          if (recpnts.size() == 1) {
              User u = recpnts.iterator().next();
              generateEnabled = getUserId().equals(u.getId()) || User.Type.CONTACT == u.getType();
          }
          target.add(
                  dialog.getSend().setEnabled(!recpnts.isEmpty())
                  , dialog.getGenerate().setEnabled(generateEnabled)
                  );
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1519: the group branch disables the personal URL outright"
  lang java
  file openmeetings-web/src/main/java/org/apache/openmeetings/web/room/menu/RoomInvitationForm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.openmeetings.web.room.menu;

  import java.util.Collection;

  public class RoomInvitationForm extends InvitationForm {
      @Override
      protected void updateButtons(AjaxRequestTarget target) {
          if (rdi.getModelObject() == InviteeType.USER) {
              super.updateButtons(target);
          } else {
              Collection<Group> to = groups.getModelObject();
              target.add(
                      dialog.getSend().setEnabled(!to.isEmpty())
                      , dialog.getGenerate().setEnabled(false)
                      );
          }
      }
  }
  ```

